# Copy to .env at the repository root. .env is gitignored; never commit a key.
#
# WHERE THE REAL KEYS ALREADY LIVE (they have been mislaid once, 2026-09-19):
#
#   local   <this repo>/.env                  gitignored, chmod 600
#   box     /etc/overdraft-guard.env          root-owned, 0600
#
# The box copy is deliberately NOT in deploy.sh's rsync list; it is placed by
# hand, once. deploy/overdraft-guard.service reads it with
# `EnvironmentFile=-/etc/overdraft-guard.env`, and the leading `-` makes it
# OPTIONAL — a box without that file starts happily with no keys and degrades in
# silence. If the explainer is off in production, look there first.
#
# The Gemini key spent an afternoon lost because it had been written only into
# the gemini-chat worktree's own .env (Desktop/vthacks-gemini/.env) and never
# into the main checkout. Worktrees do not share gitignored files. Before
# reissuing a key that seems to have vanished, check the other worktrees.

# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey. The free tier is enough for a
# demo — do NOT set up billing. Current keys begin "AQ.", older ones "AIza".
# Copy it with the copy icon on the key row: the page only ever shows the last
# four characters, and "gen-lang-client-..." is the PROJECT id, not the key.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Optional. Any current text model id works; see https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash
# Optional, but wanted. Tried in order when the model above is overloaded.
# Without these a busy gemini-3.8-flash is a dead chat feature: the live check on
# 2026-09-19 returned "This model is currently experiencing high demand" on the
# first attempt and succeeded on the retry.
GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODELS=gemini-3.5-flash,gemini-2.5-flash
# Optional. Seconds to wait for Gemini before answering 502.
GEMINI_TIMEOUT_S=25

# Nessie, the Capital One banking sandbox. Key from nessieisreal.com via GitHub
# login. It travels as a QUERY PARAMETER (?key=...), so nothing may log a full
# URL.
#
# Verified 2026-09-19: a WRONG key returns 200 [] — indistinguishable from a
# valid key over an empty sandbox — and a MISSING key returns 502 with a generic
# message. There is no 401 and no 403, so a read can never confirm the key is
# good. Credentials are checked write-then-read instead.
NESSIE_API_KEY=
# Optional. Both documented hosts answer identically; the interactive reference
# selects this one.
NESSIE_BASE_URL=https://prod-api.nessieisreal.com
# Optional. Seconds to wait for Nessie before giving up. POST /api/accounts/nessie
# answers 503 when the sandbox cannot be reached, and the page offers the
# modelled account instead; see docs/features/nessie.md.
NESSIE_TIMEOUT_S=20
# Optional. An account id already seeded into the sandbox. Set it and
# POST /api/accounts/nessie reads that account instead of creating a customer on
# every call: no writes, and nothing new left behind in someone else's sandbox.
# Creates here are permanent (DELETE answers 403), so this is the setting to use
# for judging. Seed once, copy the account_id out of the response, put it here.
NESSIE_ACCOUNT_ID=
